{
  "startedAt": "2026-10-16T02:04:38.928Z",
  "steps": [
    "A current track is cloned with a new stable identity and the same resource/settings, without adding cues. A cue is explicitly rebound before removing its old track. Chinese/English/Japanese at 390px preserve all inputs and visible controls; review and Cancel leave both the draft and author tree unchanged.",
    "Apply changes only the ordinary unsaved source draft. Ordinary Save updates exactly the reviewed audio JSON; metadata, scene, referenced WAV and other author files remain byte-identical.",
    "Saved tracks reopen with the new stable clone identity and the removed track absent. Old cue identities remain and the new stop cue targets the clone; shared Rust sampling confirms both tracks stop at 0.5 seconds.",
    "The same scene plans, builds and runs through real Godot. The host validates the two current tracks and four audio commands: music play, cloned effect play, then both stops at 0.5 seconds, with independent actor/audio completion.",
    "Chrome downloads the generated engine project ZIP. Independent verification confirms one deduplicated WAV resource, extraction preserves its exact bytes and settings, and fresh Godot import/run at another path produces identical audio events."
  ],
